B.ye=new A.O("where","Where were you around 11 last night?","On the telephone on the landing, darling, from ten to eleven until half past. Madame Leine was describing the new spring hats in exhaustive detail.",B.f,B.f)
B.y6=new A.O("about","Tell me about Mrs. Senclair.","Aunt \xc9claire was a sweet old thing with a very hard glaze. Yes, I inherit. No, I didn't do it. I look dreadful in black.",B.f,B.f)
B.Yu=new A.O("suspect","Who do you suspect?","Graham, darling. He's been sour as lemon curd for a month. Something about a reference. It's always the quiet, square ones.",B.f,B.f)
B.I_=s(["graham/alone"],t.s)
B.Yb=new A.O("concertina","Graham says he was playing the concertina.","Is THAT what it was? Wheeze, squawk, wheeze, for a solid half hour \u2014 I had a finger in my other ear to hear Madame Leine. It never stopped once, until I heard the Colonel boom \u201cWhose move is it?\u201d",B.f,B.I_)
B.Im=s(["phone"],t.s)
B.Y0=new A.O("footsteps","Did anyone pass you on the landing?","Not a soul, darling. I was draped over that telephone table for forty minutes and the only thing that came up those stairs was that dreadful music.",B.Im,B.f)
B.IX=s(["will"],t.s)
B.yc=new A.O("will","The will leaves everything to you.","And it has for ten years, darling. If I were going to do it for the money, I'd hardly have sat through a decade of her bridge parties first.",B.IX,B.f)
B.Hu=s(["bills"],t.s)
B.y1=new A.O("bills","You owe Madame Leine a fortune.","Darling, I have owed Madame Leine since I was a ladyfinger. She is far too fond of me to press. Final demands are simply how she says hello.",B.Hu,B.f)
B.k3=new A.O("cocoa","Your cocoa is all over the wine rack.","I went down for the port at nine, darling. Graham wrote it in his little book. Auntie was alive and scolding me for it at ten.",B.iD,B.f)
B.Ih=s([B.ye,B.y6,B.Yu,B.Yb,B.Y0,B.yc,B.y1,B.k3],t.q)
B.yb=new A.O("where","Where were you around 11 last night?","Out in the greenhouse 'til midnight, coverin' the strawberries against the frost. Penny let me in \u2014 door was latched. Left me boots on the mat like she always nags me to.",B.f,B.f)
B.jS=new A.O("about","Tell me about Mrs. Senclair.","She had a sharp tongue, but she let me sleep by the boiler when the potting shed leaks. Can't say fairer than that.",B.f,B.f)
B.Xo=new A.O("suspect","Who do you suspect?","Penny's got a grudge against the old girl that's older than I am. Somethin' about a recipe. And she's the one with the rollin' pins.",B.f,B.f)
B.Ip=s(["pinboiler"],t.s)
B.Xk=new A.O("pin","There was a rolling pin hidden behind your boiler.","Not mine, guv! When I got in at midnight the boiler room door was hangin' open, and I always shut it to keep the warm in. Whoever stashed that did it before I was back.",B.Ip,B.f)
B.FJ=s(["graham/latch"],t.s)
B.jU=new A.O("lockedout","Graham latches the doors at ten.","Too right he does. I hammered on the back door a good while before Penny came and let me in.",B.f,B.FJ)
B.HA=s(["dismissal"],t.s)
B.jX=new A.O("dismissal","She was going to dismiss you.","Aye, at month end. Told me herself on Monday. Month end, guv \u2014 that's three more weeks of wages and a warm boiler. Why'd I cut that short?",B.HA,B.f)
B.IK=s(["spade"],t.s)
B.jZ=new A.O("spade","What is that on your spade?","Beetroot, guv. Been liftin' beets all week. Lick it if you don't believe me. ...Suit yourself.",B.IK,B.f)
B.jW=new A.O("jam","Did you spill something in the pantry?","Dropped a crate of Penny's jam Tuesday. She ain't forgiven me, and the floor ain't neither.",B.mK,B.f)
