B.DA=new A.aA("tin","Empty Cake Tin","pantry",1,"A large tin on the pantry shelf labelled \u201cSenclair Christmas Fruitcake \u2014 12 years old. DO NOT EAT.\u201d The tin is empty. A ring in the dust shows it was lifted down very recently.",B.EL,B.h7)
B.DF=new A.aA("scoresheet","Chess Scoresheet","parlor",0,"Graham's meticulous record of last night's game. A move is entered every two or three minutes from 10:32 until 11:58 without a break, each one initialled by both players.",B.mj,B.aF)
B.HF=s([B.DA,B.ip,B.ij,B.m4,B.DF],t.F)
B.E4=new A.aA("underdrip","Sauce Beneath the Body","cellar",1,"The officers marked this where they lifted the remains: a drop of red berry sauce on the flagstones UNDERNEATH where Mrs. Senclair lay. It was on the floor before she fell on it.",B.bN,B.hk)
B.BI=new A.i(1,0.5568627450980392,0.1411764705882353,0.12549019607843137,B.d)
B.DY=new A.aA("drydrip","Dried Sauce Drip","cellar",2,"A drop of red berry sauce beside the outline, dried to a dark, cracked crust. The drips at the top of the stairs from this morning would still be glossy; this one is hours older.",B.bN,B.BI)
B.HD=s([B.E4,B.DY],t.F)
B.EY=new A.b2(984312,"MaterialIcons",!1)
B.Bm=new A.i(1,1,0.9529411764705882,0.8784313725490196,B.d)
B.DT=new A.aA("eggs","Egg Basket","kitchen",4,"The egg basket on the counter, with yesterday's delivery slip: \u201c1 dozen, fresh.\u201d All twelve eggs are still in it. A Needy Souffl\xe9 takes six.",B.EY,B.Bm)
B.EI=new A.b2(57994,"MaterialIcons",!1)
B.DK=new A.aA("ovenash","Cold Oven","kitchen",2,"The kitchen oven. The firebox holds nothing but old grey ash, cold right through, and the coal scuttle beside it is full to the brim.",B.EI,B.lp)
B.Id=s([B.DT,B.DK],t.F)
B.Ea=new A.aA("retire","Letter to an Agency","study",0,"On Mrs. Senclair's desk, ready to post: \u201cPlease send a modern housekeeper at once. The present one, P. Cotta, is to be retired without notice or pension. She makes the same puddings she made thirty years ago.\u201d",B.cn,B.aF)
B.Ge=s([B.ik,B.Ea],t.F)
B.DJ=new A.aA("cakesack","Christmas Fruitcake","pantry",3,"Pushed deep into a flour sack: a fruitcake as hard as granite. One corner is freshly chipped, and there is custard on it.",B.bb,B.at)
B.E6=new A.aA("cakecrate","Christmas Fruitcake","storage",1,"At the bottom of a crate of old curtains: a fruitcake as hard as granite. One corner is freshly chipped, and there is custard on it.",B.bb,B.at)
B.HC=s([B.DJ,B.E6],t.F)
B.G4=s([B.iG,B.HD,B.Id,B.Ge,B.HC],t.Rt)
B.E9=new A.aA("regiment","Letter from the Regiment","study",5,"In the desk drawer, a reply to Mrs. Senclair from Fort Fondant: \u201cMadam, we regret that we can find no record of any Colonel Cannoli among our fighting officers, nor of the medals you describe.\u201d",B.cn,B.aF)
B.E2=new A.aA("ricottadrip","White Cream Drips","entrance",4,"A few spots of thick white ricotta on the floor at the top of the cellar steps, dried at the edges.",B.bN,B.i)
B.J3=s([B.m6,B.m5,B.m7,B.E9,B.iq,B.ig,B.io,B.ii,B.im,B.ih,B.il,B.m9,B.E2],t.F)
B.XB=new A.O("what","What happened to her?","Victim is Mrs. \xc9claire Senclair, founder of Senclair Confections. Struck from behind, once, with something heavy. She went down like a dropped tray. We traced where she fell in powdered sugar.",B.f,B.f)
B.Xn=new A.O("weapon","What was the weapon?","Dense, blunt, about the size of a brick. We picked raisins and candied peel out of the, er, point of impact. Fruitcake, Detective. An old one. One dessert could swing it.",B.f,B.f)
B.I1=s([B.XB,B.Xn,B.k2],t.q)
B.IQ=s(["underdrip"],t.s)
B.Yp=new A.O("under","There was sauce underneath the body.","I noted that myself when we moved her. Whatever dripped there, dripped before she hit the floor, or as she did. Nobody slid it under her afterwards.",B.IQ,B.f)
B.HB=s(["drydrip"],t.s)
B.Yd=new A.O("dry","How long does berry sauce take to dry like that?","Fresh sauce stays tacky a couple of hours. That spot was bone dry and cracked when we arrived at seven, and the housekeeper says she only came down at half six.",B.HB,B.f)
B.Fn=s([B.yf,B.y3,B.y8,B.y9,B.Yp,B.Yd],t.q)
B.IR=s(["underdrip","drydrip"],t.s)
B.XJ=new A.O("sauce","There is red berry sauce beside the body.","Well, of course it is. I told you \u2014 I went all to pieces when I found her this morning, and my topping runs when I'm upset.",B.IR,B.f)
B.IO=s(["tin"],t.s)
B.Xh=new A.O("tin","The Christmas fruitcake is gone from its tin.","Gone? Twelve years that thing has sat up there. Madam wouldn't let me throw it out. Well, the pantry is never locked, Detective. Anybody could have reached it down.",B.IO,B.f)
B.HE=s(["eggs"],t.s)
B.Yl=new A.O("eggs","All twelve of yesterday's eggs are still in the basket.","I used up last week's eggs first. Waste not, want not.",B.HE,B.f)
B.mU=s(["ovenash"],t.s)
B.XH=new A.O("oven","Your oven is stone cold and the coal has not been touched.","I always sweep out the grate the moment I've finished baking. And I had coal left over from the day before. Habit, Detective.",B.mU,B.f)
B.GR=s(["barry/window"],t.s)
B.YB=new A.O("window","Barry says the kitchen was empty at eleven.","Barry was half frozen and seeing things. I may have stepped into the scullery for sugar. For a moment.",B.f,B.GR)
B.GM=s(["tira/smell"],t.s)
B.Yo=new A.O("smell","Tira says there was no smell of baking last night.","Miss Tira had a telephone pressed to one side of her head and the Colonel's cigar up the other. I shouldn't rely on her nose.",B.f,B.GM)
B.ID=s(["retire"],t.s)
B.Xw=new A.O("retire","She was going to retire you without notice.","Was she? She said nothing to me. Thirty years, and the same puddings \u2014 well. They were good enough to build her a factory.",B.ID,B.f)
B.Fq=s([B.jT,B.y7,B.yg,B.XJ,B.Xh,B.Yl,B.XH,B.YB,B.Yo,B.Xw,B.jR,B.jY,B.k0,B.jV],t.q)
B.Y6=new A.O("where","Where were you around 11 last night?","In the parlor, sir, at chess with the Colonel, from half past ten until midnight. Neither of us left the board.",B.f,B.f)
B.Ys=new A.O("sheet","Your scoresheet shows no breaks at all.","Every move timed and initialled by both players, sir. The Colonel insists upon it, as he believes that I cheat. I believe the same of him. It makes for an honest record.",B.eJ,B.f)
B.Gs=s(["penny/eggs"],t.s)
B.Y_=new A.O("eggs","Would Penny bake with last week's eggs?","Mrs. Cotta, sir? Never. There were no eggs left from last week; I signed for the new dozen yesterday because the larder was bare. And she permits nothing but the freshest. She says a souffl\xe9 knows.",B.f,B.Gs)
B.XG=new A.O("brandy","There is ricotta at the top of the cellar steps.","The Colonel fetched up his own brandy at eight o'clock, sir, rather than ring for me. I disapproved, and entered it in the cellar book.",B.iI,B.f)
B.Gm=s([B.Y6,B.jP,B.ya,B.Ys,B.Y_,B.XG,B.jQ,B.k_,B.k1],t.q)
B.Yf=new A.O("sheet","You initialled every move on Graham's scoresheet.","Had to, sir. The fellow moves his bishops when one blinks. Never took my eyes off him in an hour and a half. He'll tell you the same of me, the cheek of it.",B.eJ,B.f)
B.Y1=new A.O("drip","You left ricotta at the top of the cellar steps.","Went down for a decent brandy at eight, sir. Graham pours like a miser. \xc9claire was alive and well and telling me so at supper.",B.iI,B.f)
B.IC=s(["regiment"],t.s)
B.XS=new A.O("regiment","Fort Fondant has never heard of you.","Not among the FIGHTING officers, no. I was a colonel in the Catering Corps, sir. Forty years of trifle for the troops. One doesn't advertise it. \xc9claire knew, and teased me rotten.",B.IC,B.f)
B.GF=s([B.yh,B.y2,B.y4,B.Yf,B.Y1,B.yd,B.XS,B.y5],t.q)
B.Xu=new A.O("suspect","Who do you suspect?","Graham and the Colonel, darling, thick as thieves over that chessboard. Each one swears the other never moved. How convenient.",B.f,B.f)
B.XK=new A.O("check","Could the chess players have slipped out?","I only wish they had, darling. The Colonel bellowed \u201cCHECK!\u201d up the stairwell every few minutes the whole time I was on the telephone, and Graham sniffed after every one. It was like a metronome. Neither of them drew breath long enough to murder anyone.",B.f,B.iH)
B.mJ=s(["penny/where"],t.s)
B.Xm=new A.O("smell","Penny was baking a souffl\xe9 at that hour.","Was she? How odd. When Penny bakes, the whole stairwell reeks of it for hours. Last night I smelt nothing but the Colonel's cigar.",B.f,B.mJ)
B.Hr=s([B.ye,B.y6,B.Xu,B.XK,B.Xm,B.yc,B.y1,B.k3],t.q)
B.XE=new A.O("where","Where were you around 11 last night?","Out in the greenhouse 'til midnight, coverin' the strawberries against the frost. Came up to the house the once, about eleven, after me tea flask, but the door was latched so I went back. Penny let me in at midnight.",B.f,B.f)
B.XM=new A.O("suspect","Who do you suspect?","That Colonel owes her a packet, and Miss Tira gets the lot. Take your pick, guv.",B.f,B.f)
B.Yw=new A.O("window","Penny says she never left her oven.","Does she? When I came up at eleven I looked in the kitchen window, hopin' she'd pass me flask out. Lamp lit, oven dark, no Penny. I stood there a good five minutes. Thought she'd gone to bed.",B.f,B.mJ)
B.YA=new A.O("coal","The kitchen coal scuttle is still full.","'Course it is, I filled it at six like every evenin'. If it's still full this mornin', nobody's fired that oven. An hour's bakin' burns half of it.",B.mU,B.f)
B.GE=s(["penny/oven"],t.s)
B.XV=new A.O("leftover","Penny says she had coal left from the day before.","Not a lump, guv. She was scrapin' the bottom when I filled it \u2014 said so herself, and none too kindly.",B.f,B.GE)
B.Gr=s([B.XE,B.jS,B.XM,B.Yw,B.YA,B.XV,B.jU,B.jX,B.jZ,B.jW],t.q)
